-- title:
--   Branches over the Γ₀(qM') Gauss place are conjugates of W₀, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ for which some ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carries $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Inside $\mathrm{Laurent}(L)$ consider three intermediate fields: $K$, the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$; $K_0$, generated likewise from the $\Gamma_0(M')$-field; and $K_0'$, generated likewise from the $\Gamma_0(qM')$-field; with $K_0 \le K_0' \le K$ and $K_0 \le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$. Let $W_0 \subseteq K$, $O_0 \subseteq K_0$, $O_0' \subseteq K_0'$ be the valuation subrings cut out by the Gauss condition: $f$ belongs to the ring exactly when $f\,y = x$ in $\mathrm{Laurent}(L)$ for some power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. The assertion is that for every valuation subring $B$ of $K$ whose contraction to $K_0'$ is $O_0'$, firstly there is an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ fixing $K_0'$ pointwise with $B = \tau^{-1}(W_0)$, and secondly the contraction of $B$ to $K_0$ equals $O_0$ and, for the resulting extension $O_0 \to B$, the ramification index of the maximal ideal of $O_0$ in the maximal ideal of $B$ equals $1$ and $O_0 \to B$ is a local homomorphism with separable residue field extension $\kappa(B)/\kappa(O_0)$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case of the local analysis, at the Gauss ($\infty$-type) place of the $\Gamma_0(M')$ floor, of the places of the level-$q^2M'$ modular function field lying over a prescribed place of the $\Gamma_0(qM')$ floor: such places form a single orbit under the $L$-automorphisms of $K$ fixing $K_0'$, and each is unramified with separable residue extension over the floor. It is used in the proofs that the relevant height-one places of $X_H$ are unramified.
